Steam Discord Rich Presence (rpc-bridge, works with the 1.4.1.2 bridge.exe)
 - rpc-bridge-bin 1.4.1.3 quits on Proton (wine 11.0 has no AF_UNIX and it now insists on Staging); 1.4.1.2 falls back to syscalls.
   1.4.1.2 is hand-copied over /opt/rpc-bridge/bridge.exe for now, so a package update undoes it. Pin it in the dotfiles.
 - Steam started from a terminal (tmux) lacks the variables; start it from walker or after login
 - Flatpak Discord cannot see host processes, so game-presence (.local/bin, user service) starts a stand-in process named after the game
   inside Discord's sandbox (flatpak run --parent-share-pids). Works for Overwatch (Registered Games shows it); check it counts for the badges
   Games Discord lists without executables (MECCHA CHAMELEON) get a stand-in named after the game from its Steam app id; Discord detects that by name
 - ultrawide notification popups sit at 75% of the width (notification-position.sh); check they move back on the other monitors
 - launch a Proton game with Discord open and check it shows in Discord
 - log: tail ~/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/compatdata/*/pfx/drive_c/windows/logs/bridge.log
 - turn off per game: PROTON_REMOTE_DEBUG_CMD= %command%
